title: A Very Present Help – Trusting God in Trouble
description: Trusting God in trouble: what affliction is for, God our refuge and strength, waiting on the Lord, fear is a lack of faith, and vengeance is the Lord's, from the teachings on trusting God in trouble.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-trust.html
highlight: trust

# One deck for the topic "Trusting God in trouble" (122 teachings), its five themes given equal weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.

=== Introduction
--- A Very Present Help [title]
overline: Doctrine · Trusting God in trouble
heading: A Very Present Help
sub: Affliction, comfort, and waiting on the Lord.
refs: Psalms 46:1; Romans 8:28; Isaiah 40:31; Philippians 4:6-7; Romans 12:19
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 17950, 17949
--- God is our refuge and strength
big: Psalms 46:1 | mark: a very present help in trouble
xr: Proverbs 18:10 | The name of the LORD is a strong tower: the righteous runneth into it, and is safe.
xr: Isaiah 41:10 | Fear thou not; for I am with thee: be not dismayed; for I am thy God.
xr: Nahum 1:7 | The LORD is good, a strong hold in the day of trouble.
p: These are not platitudes or empty promises. These are real and observable and heartfelt understandings and expressions of faith, forged in troubled times. And in any Christian life, given enough time, this is proven to us again and again.
read: app:doctrine-trust~17949 | God is our refuge and strength

=== Affliction and its purpose
# from 17924, 17926
--- Counted as sheep for the slaughter
kicker: Affliction
big: Romans 8:36-37 | mark: we are more than conquerors through him that loved us
p: What makes Psalm 44 so jarring is that the congregation is stating they are not being punished for apostasy ([[Psalms 44:17]]). Travails come upon the just. Upon the faithful who have placed their trust in the Lord.
p: Because man is naturally going to complain in the best of times, we need to be prepared for the proper attitude in the worst. To be persuaded that nothing can separate us from the love of Christ. Even when things are bleak.

# from 17880, 17883, 17889, 11161
--- Why art thou cast down?
kicker: Affliction
big: Psalms 42:11 | mark: hope thou in God: for I shall yet praise him
p: It is a comfort to any believer to realize that remembering past deliverances doesn't automatically cure present depression. As Pastor Jack Hyles often preached, you can't have unshakable faith unless your faith has been shaken.
p: Faith isn't the absence of trouble; it is the stubborn decision to anchor oneself to the Rock when you feel like you are drowning. In the moment, it's okay to *say unto God my rock, Why hast thou forgotten me?* Just don't take this feeling as an excuse to forget God.
p: Aaron held his peace, but he was still grieved ([[Leviticus 10:19-20]]). God is understanding that sometimes the truth of His word is bitter to us, in the flesh. He is patient.

# from 11255, 1668, 16853, 16130
--- Neither hath this man sinned
kicker: Affliction
big: John 9:3 | mark: Neither hath this man sinned, nor his parents: but that the works of God should be made manifest in him
p: Man has the gift of pattern recognition, and it is hard not to see that the fates that befall others must be in answer to their sin. Jesus rebuked the people doing this ([[Luke 13:1-5]]). Some things are just chance ([[Ecclesiastes 9:11]]).
p: Job's friends defend retribution theology rigorously, the idea of karma in God's doings. This line of thought is just as common today. But not God's ([[Job 42:7]]). We shouldn't assume every bad thing that happens to another is for their own sin. Lazarus' suffering on earth wasn't in vain ([[Luke 16:25]]).

# from 16849, 16843, 13566
--- My grace is sufficient
kicker: Affliction
big: 2 Corinthians 12:9 | mark: My grace is sufficient for thee: for my strength is made perfect in weakness
p: *Shall we receive good at the hand of God, and shall we not receive evil?* And Job sinned not with his lips ([[Job 2:10]]). Whether we are blessed or cursed, all is to His glory.
p: This. I cannot tell you what this truth of God's word feels like, you have to experience it. When there is trouble and you think you cannot go on, you turn to the Lord and He carries you there, to where you need to be.

# from 13593, 17833, 12868
--- Tribulation worketh patience
kicker: Affliction
big: Romans 5:3-4 | mark: knowing that tribulation worketh patience
p: The harder the times, the more likely the people turn to the Lord. The better the times, the quicker they fall away ([[Judges 3:1-4]]). God uses tribulation to prove us. That we may learn to trust Him more.
p: *Many are the afflictions of the righteous: but the LORD delivereth him out of them all* ([[Psalms 34:19]]). We are not promised a carefree life. You cannot be delivered by God from tribulation, without tribulation.

# from 17154, 10082, 8755
--- Whom the Lord loveth
kicker: Affliction
big: Proverbs 3:11-12 | mark: For whom the LORD loveth he correcteth
p: Many new Christians become frustrated that when they got saved, they still had to endure the pain and hard work of getting up out of the hole their old man had dug for them with their sin. But that hole was a grave. And God has given us the rope to climb out of it.
p: Where we slip, know it is God's correction, rebuking those sons whom He loves. We must not despise the rod of correction given us by our Father, but take joy in that He loves us ([[Hebrews 12:1-2]]).

# from 9864, 3998
--- The more they afflicted them
kicker: Affliction
big: Exodus 1:12 | mark: the more they afflicted them, the more they multiplied and grew
p: In the days of the Hebrews in Egypt, of Jesus' ministry on Earth, of the early churches, persecution led to the greatest gains for God. We are given trials because God has considered us worthy to endure ([[2 Corinthians 4:8-9]]).
p: In our tribulations we have comfort, given by God's grace, and in that comfort, the ability to give the same comfort to others in need ([[2 Corinthians 1:4]]).

# from 17695, 9969, 9966, 11932
--- A sweet savour of Christ
kicker: Affliction
big: 2 Timothy 3:12 | mark: all that will live godly in Christ Jesus shall suffer persecution
p: A younger sister in Christ just won someone to the Lord, and within a few days was being afflicted from all sides. It was good to give her this perspective. To patiently endure it, and see her faith grow.
p: The elders of Israel said to Moses, *ye have made our savour to be abhorred in the eyes of Pharaoh* ([[Exodus 5:21]]). To the world, we stink like death, because we remind them that they are perishing, but our obedience to God in Christ is a sweet savour unto the Lord ([[2 Corinthians 2:15-16]]).

# from 10159, 17877
--- Hands held up
kicker: Affliction
big: Exodus 17:12 | mark: Aaron and Hur stayed up his hands
p: We may grow weary. Our arms may fall. But surrounding ourselves with fellow believers, the brethren who will help hold up our arms, and the rock that is Jesus Christ, to rest on, we will be victorious.
p: We often face betrayal at the most inopportune times. Jesus knows what it is like to be betrayed by those closest to Him ([[John 13:18]]). *There is a friend that sticketh closer than a brother* ([[Proverbs 18:24]]). That friend is Jesus Christ.
