read: app:doctrine-trust~14751 | Yet I will rejoice in the Lord

=== Waiting on the Lord
# from 13365, 17711, 17772
--- They that wait upon the LORD
kicker: Waiting on the Lord
big: Isaiah 40:31 | mark: they that wait upon the LORD shall renew their strength
p: Psalm 13 captures a very real feeling of the Christian life, the impatient waiting for God's perfect timing, turning into an acknowledgement that He has dealt bountifully with us ([[Psalms 13:5-6]]).
p: *The Lord is not slack concerning his promise, as some men count slackness* ([[2 Peter 3:9]]). In our patience, God gives us added strength. They that wait on Him shall not be ashamed ([[Psalms 25:3]]).

# from 12254
--- New every morning
kicker: Waiting on the Lord
big: Lamentations 3:22-23 | mark: They are new every morning: great is thy faithfulness
p: We are called to pick up our cross every day, so if we stumble and backslide, if we turn to the left or the right, God is merciful in calling us back to the straight paths.
p: *It is good that a man should both hope and quietly wait for the salvation of the Lord* ([[Lamentations 3:26]]).

# from 12880, 16710, 12875
--- Not forcing the issue
kicker: Waiting on the Lord
big: Deuteronomy 1:42 | mark: Go not up, neither fight; for I am not among you
p: Rather than accept the chastisement, they tried to defeat the Amorites themselves, only to be driven out, as bees do. When their children went to war, 38 years later, on God's schedule, they easily defeated them ([[Numbers 21:23-24]]).
p: It is entirely about faith, patience and meekness. Not taking matters into our own hands. Accepting that the Lord may deny us something now, that we have something better later.
p: There is also a fine line between faith and tempting God ([[Ezra 8:22]]; [[Matthew 4:7]]). Maybe the offer of help itself came from God.

# from 13519, 3859
--- How long, O Lord?
kicker: Waiting on the Lord
big: Revelation 6:10-11 | mark: that they should rest yet for a little season
p: Many, frustrated by the world, express impatience with those of us who profess Christ. That we should *do something!* They complain that God is too long suffering for them.
p: The saints slain for the word plead with God to pour out His wrath on the wicked, and are told to rest a while more, and they do. We should learn to be a bit more patient with God.
p: *There failed not ought of any good thing which the LORD had spoken* ([[Joshua 21:45]]).

# from 3341, 5009, 4117
--- Not sedition, but faith
kicker: Waiting on the Lord
big: Romans 8:28 | mark: all things work together for good to them that love God
p: We need not sow sedition or take up arms or anything else but have faith in God. Often Christians get impatient with God, and try to take vengeance into their own hands. Reactionary spirals, further worsening the conditions we face. Dancing to the devil's tune.
p: There is no liberty outside of Christ. If you truly believed that when they threaten your life, they are threatening you with Heaven, you wouldn't be afraid.
p: The more you are willing to suffer and yet trust Him, the more you will gain ([[Matthew 19:29]]). I have seen it. I have been so blessed. Let go. Have faith.
read: app:doctrine-trust~17711 | Waiting on God's perfect timing
read: app:doctrine-trust~12880 | Not forcing the issue: waiting on God
read: app:doctrine-trust~3859 | Patience with God and the saints under the altar

=== Fear not
# from 4810, 4811, 17951
--- Be careful for nothing
kicker: Fear is a lack of faith
big: Philippians 4:6-7 | mark: Be careful for nothing; the peace of God, which passeth all understanding
p: This should be the default state of your Christian life. Joy, not worrying and fearful for the cares of this world but trusting, in prayer and supplication, in thanksgiving.
p: For me, it was fear and concerns of this world that led me consistently to misery, anger and resentment. Fear for family, work, relationships with others... all things work for good when you love God and trust Him, thankful regardless of outcome. Just have to let go.

# from 17850, 8723
--- Fret not
kicker: Fear is a lack of faith
big: Psalms 37:1 | mark: Fret not thyself because of evildoers
p: God has built us in a way that makes our gratitude for what we have the source for being less anxious. It is impossible for those that are truly grateful to God for their station in life, and the protection of His mighty hand, to fret.
p: *In every thing give thanks* ([[1 Thessalonians 5:18]]). This one exercise will change your life as profoundly as anything short of salvation. I testify to it, God is my witness.

# from 13630, 13617, 13618
--- Help thou mine unbelief
kicker: Fear is a lack of faith
big: Mark 9:24 | mark: Lord, I believe; help thou mine unbelief
p: We often search for faith in our tribulation, not because we doubt God, but we have doubts about ourselves. Gideon wanted a sign, and the Lord said, *have not I sent thee?* ([[Judges 6:14]]) How often, when we know the right thing to do, but are afraid, do we place the burden on the Lord to show us a sign?
p: Gideon tore down his father's altar, by night, *because he feared his father's household* ([[Judges 6:27]]). Often the only hindrance to doing something great for the Lord is our own fear.

# from 11721, 11740, 1260
--- Running with the footmen
kicker: Fear is a lack of faith
big: Jeremiah 12:5 | mark: If thou hast run with the footmen, and they have wearied thee, then how canst thou contend with horses?
p: If we, in the land of peace wherein we've trusted, can't handle things, what will we do when the river floods? So many Christians constantly complain about how “persecuted” they feel.
p: If you are walking the best you can in the spirit, and still find yourself fearful and angry all the time, snapping at others, there's something wrong with your Christian walk. If what you're consuming online leaves you more afraid, stop engaging in it. Fear is a sin.

# from 8084
--- Faith over fear
kicker: Fear is a lack of faith
big: Revelation 12:11 | mark: they loved not their lives unto the death
p: We may be cut off from buying and selling for refusing the mark of the beast. All our preparing and stockpiling won't save us. But faith can.
p: It's easy to fall into fear at being cast out into the wilderness. But there in the wilderness is where God provides. Manna from heaven. Fed by ravens. Water from flint ([[Revelation 12:14]]). Faith over fear.
read: app:doctrine-trust~4810 | Be careful for nothing
read: app:doctrine-trust~17850 | Fret not: gratitude casts out anxiety
read: app:doctrine-trust~13617 | Have not I sent thee?
read: app:doctrine-trust~1260 | Fear is a sin: step away from what feeds it

=== Vengeance is the Lord's
# from 17292
--- A just man falleth seven times
kicker: Vengeance is the Lord's
big: Proverbs 24:16-17 | mark: a just man falleth seven times, and riseth up again; Rejoice not when thine enemy falleth
p: We may fall in our Christian walk, multiple times, but we rise up again. Knowing this, we are admonished against taking pleasure in the fall of the wicked. In their fall is revealed His wrath, but it also is the opportunity to show His mercy and give the truth of the gospel, through us.
p: We should not worry and fret about what evil men do, nor be envious of the wicked. God will repay.

# from 16691, 10970
--- We are the servants of God
kicker: Vengeance is the Lord's
big: Ezra 5:11 | mark: We are the servants of the God of heaven and earth
p: When we are accused, we should not be afraid, nor proudly stand up, nor in fear kowtow and cease our efforts. Humbly and honestly stand for what we believe in. When an apartment manager threatens to call the police on soul winners, don't argue. Trust Him to deliver you.
p: God in His grace and love promises us one more thing; vengeance. He will repay ([[2 Thessalonians 1:6-7]]). We aren't floor mats to be trampled on. God will always deliver.
read: app:doctrine-trust~17292 | A just man falleth seven times and riseth
read: app:doctrine-trust~16691 | We are the servants of God
read: app:doctrine-trust~10970 | God will repay those who persecute His saints

=== Great is thy faithfulness
--- Great Is Thy Faithfulness [title]
overline: Trusting God in trouble
heading: Great Is Thy Faithfulness
big: Isaiah 41:10 | mark: Fear thou not; for I am with thee
center: The Lord God is my strength. Whatever is troubling you, He is there to help you.
